<edge source="strait_hormuz_standoff::passage_control" target="currency_market_shock::exchange_rate_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in asserted passage control raises perceived sovereign and trade-risk, triggering FX hedging, forward-point dislocations and capital flight that produce increased directional pressure on affected exchange rates.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="strait_hormuz_standoff::passage_control" target="global_ai_competition::regulatory_constraint" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stricter control over the chokepoint raises geopolitical and national‑security concerns among states, accelerating export controls, supply‑chain vetting and tighter rules on cross‑border AI-related technology transfers and investments.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">global_ai_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="strait_hormuz_standoff::passage_control" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp increase in asserted passage control (blockades, checkpoints, stricter rules of passage) forces allies to choose between military countermeasures and protecting energy/diplomatic links, producing visible policy splits and reducing coordinated allied responses on the Russia‑Ukraine file.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="strait_hormuz_standoff::passage_control" target="us_china_econ_rivalry::onshore_mfg_capacity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A stronger assertion of maritime passage control (inspections, restrictions or blockades) raises perceived supply‑chain vulnerability, triggering government subsidies, procurement guarantees and private investment to expand domestic advanced‑manufacturing capacity.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_econ_rivalry</data>
