  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in hostile or disruptive maritime incidents elevates bilateral risk perceptions and political pressure, prompting faster imposition or tightening of export controls and licensing on dual‑use maritime, communications and navigation technologies between the US and China.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_econ_rivalry</data>
</edge>
