<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="currency_market_shock::short_rate_expectations" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter political coordination among allies produces more effective sanctions and coordinated energy restrictions that push near‑term inflation and policy tightening odds higher, leading markets to price in an elevated short‑rate path.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">currency_market_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="global_ai_competition::regulatory_constraint" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger political cohesion among allies enables coordinated policy actions—such as harmonized export controls and joint oversight on dual-use technologies—that increase the intensity and scope of regulatory constraints on AI activities.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_ai_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="strait_hormuz_standoff::passage_control" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Improved political coordination among allied states leads to synchronized naval tasking orders, common rules of transit and combined checkpoint/escort operations that increase the degree of asserted control over transit through the chokepoint.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="strait_hormuz_standoff::rerouting_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger allied political agreement produces coordinated security assurances, convoying and insurance guarantees that reduce commercial incentives for shippers to divert around the Strait, lowering the vessel rerouting rate.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" target="us_china_econ_rivalry::export_control_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher political cohesion among US and allied governments produces coordinated policy decisions to tighten and harmonize export controls on sensitive dual‑use and defense‑adjacent technologies, raising overall export control intensity vis‑à‑vis strategic competitors.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_econ_rivalry</data>
</edge>
