  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained spikes in prices for critical inputs increase production costs and depress manufacturing output and transport fuel demand in major importers, leading to reduced crude import requirements and a drop in net crude flows through Hormuz.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">us_china_econ_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
