<edge source="currency_market_shock::exchange_rate_pressure" target="global_ai_competition::financial_liquidity_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp exchange-rate depreciation raises the local-currency cost of dollar-denominated cloud services and external debt servicing for AI firms, draining cash buffers and reducing available liquid funding for operations and development.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">global_ai_competition</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_market_shock::exchange_rate_pressure" target="russia_ukraine_war::drone_attack_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Directional pressure that weakens local currencies versus major suppliers raises the cost of imported sensors, motors and electronics for commercial drone producers, reducing production rates and thereby decreasing the frequency of unmanned attacks that rely on those commercial supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_market_shock::exchange_rate_pressure" target="strait_hormuz_standoff::incident_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Acute exchange-rate pressure on a Gulf state's currency raises its need for foreign exchange and can prompt state-aligned actors to seize, board or harass commercial vessels and increase inspections to acquire FX or signal leverage, raising the frequency of maritime incidents.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">strait_hormuz_standoff</data>
</edge>
<edge source="currency_market_shock::exchange_rate_pressure" target="us_china_econ_rivalry::trade_flow_goods" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An increase in exchange-rate depreciation pressure on a producing economy's currency makes its advanced-tech and mineral exports cheaper in foreign-currency terms, mechanically boosting cross-border shipments to rival markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">currency_market_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_econ_rivalry</data>
</edge>
